    <p class="tag">Core Service</p>
    <h1>Family &amp; Spousal Visas</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Keep your family together in the Philippines, with the right long-term status.</p>

    <p>Marriage to a Filipino citizen, or family ties to someone already living in the Philippines, can support a long-term immigration pathway. Foreign Immigration Services helps you understand which options apply to your family's circumstances and manages the application process.</p>

    <div class="media-split">
      <div class="media-split__media">
        {{ mediaPanel("family-spousal", "square", "light") }}
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Assessing your family's circumstances against the long-term status options available</li>
          <li>Preparing and organising the required documentation, including civil documents such as marriage certificates</li>
          <li>Managing the application and liaison with the relevant authority</li>
          <li>Advising on the ongoing obligations associated with family-based long-term status</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Common Situations We Handle</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Marriage to a Filipino citizen</li>
      <li>Bringing a spouse, partner or dependent children to join you in the Philippines</li>
      <li>Mixed-nationality families travelling together under the Balikbayan privilege</li>
      <li>Other family reunification circumstances</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the Process Works</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Initial enquiry</h3>
        <p>Tell us about your family's circumstances and plans.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Assessment</h3>
        <p>We review your circumstances and explain which options may be available.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Preparation</h3>
        <p>We help you prepare and organise the required documentation.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Submission and follow-up</h3>
        <p>We manage the application and keep you informed of its progress.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What We May Need From You</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Passports of all family members involved</li>
      <li>Civil documentation relevant to your family relationship, such as a marriage or birth certificate</li>
      <li>Details of your family's current and intended circumstances in the Philippines</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="service-cta">
      <h2>Planning a Future Together in the Philippines?</h2>
